---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What loomweaver.dev processes, on what legal basis, and which rights you have."
>
  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>The controller within the meaning of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:</p>
  <address>
    Norbert Heinz Rosenwinkel<br />
    Heinrich-Böll-Weg 21<br />
    30629 Hannover<br />
    Germany<br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:info@loomweaver.dev">info@loomweaver.dev</a>
  </address>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>With regard to your personal data, you have the following rights against us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Right of access (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
    <li>Right to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
    <li>Right to erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
    <li>Right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
    <li>Right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
    <li>Right to object to processing (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
    <li>Right to withdraw consent with effect for the future (Art. 7 (3) GDPR)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority about
    our processing of your personal data (Art. 77 GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and server log files</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted by an external service provider (STRATO AG, Otto-Ostrowski-Straße 7,
    10249 Berlin, Germany). When you visit the site, the host automatically collects data in
    so-called server log files that your browser transmits: the IP address, date and time of
    access, the requested resource, the referring page and the browser and operating system used.
  </p>
  <p>
    This data serves the technical delivery of the site, the assurance of stable and secure
    operation, and the prevention of abuse. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in a secure
    and functional service (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR). The log data is not merged with other data sources
    and is deleted after a short period unless it is needed to investigate a specific case of abuse.
  </p>
  <p>
    The same applies to the demo application at{' '}
    <a href="https://demo.loomweaver.dev/">demo.loomweaver.dev</a>, which is hosted by the same
    provider.
  </p>

  <h2>Email contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you contact us by email, the personal data transmitted with the email (your email address,
    the content of your message) is stored and processed solely for handling your enquiry. The legal
    basis is our legitimate interest in answering your enquiry (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR); if the contact
    aims at concluding a contract, additionally Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR. The data is deleted as soon as
    it is no longer required for the purpose of its collection, that is, when the respective
    conversation has ended. Statutory retention periods remain unaffected.
  </p>

  <h2>Local storage in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    So the site can remember your preferences, we store purely functional values in your browser’s
    local storage (localStorage):
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>your chosen colour scheme (<code>starlight-theme</code>)</li>
    <li>your decision on the analytics notice (<code>lw-consent</code>)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These values remain on your device, are not transmitted to us or to third parties, and serve
    solely the function of the site. This is not tracking. No consent is required for this
    technically necessary storage; the legal basis is our legitimate interest in providing a
    functional website (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR). You can delete the values at any time via your browser
    settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    The demo application at <a href="https://demo.loomweaver.dev/">demo.loomweaver.dev</a> likewise
    keeps everything you enter and configure there in your browser alone. It is not transmitted to a
    server and we cannot see it.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and web analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets no tracking cookies and embeds no advertising networks. Only the technically
    necessary localStorage values described above are stored. Fonts are served locally from our
    server; there is no connection to an external font CDN.
  </p>
  <p>
    On your first visit, a notice banner appears through which you can consent to or decline the use
    of the analytics tool Umami. Your choice is stored in your browser and respected on future
    visits. This site embeds no further third-party services.
  </p>

  <h2>Web analytics (Umami)</h2>
  <p>
    We use Umami on this website, a privacy-friendly open-source web-analytics tool. Umami is only
    loaded once you give your consent via the notice banner.
  </p>
  <p>
    Umami collects no personal data and uses no cookies. Only anonymised, aggregated data is
    recorded, such as page views, visit duration, country of origin and device type. Identifying
    individual visitors is not possible.
  </p>
  <p>
    The data is processed on servers of Umami Cloud (Umami Software Inc.). Further information can
    be found in{' '}
    <a href="https://umami.is/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Umami’s privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is your consent pursuant to Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR. You can withdraw your consent
    at any time with effect for the future:
  </p>
  <p>
    <button type="button" data-consent-revoke class="revoke">Withdraw consent</button>
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    Our site contains links to external services, such as the source code on GitHub. By clicking
    them you leave this site. We have no influence on the data processing of the linked providers;
    their respective privacy policies apply.
  </p>

  <h2>SSL/TLS encryption</h2>
  <p>
    For security reasons, this site uses SSL or TLS encryption. You can recognise an encrypted
    connection by the “https://” in your browser’s address bar.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this privacy policy</h2>
  <p>
    We will adapt this privacy policy whenever changes to the site or to the legal situation make it
    necessary. The current version published here always applies.
  </p>
</LegalPage>

<style>
  .revoke {
    padding: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    border-radius: 0.375rem;
    background-color: transparent;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .revoke:hover {
    background-color: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
  }
</style>
